# Expectation record for 13_floating_point/001_float_double_arithmetic.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 001_float_double_arithmetic
area               = 13_floating_point
description        = Single- and double-precision arithmetic in a folded and a volatile-runtime variant of every operation: add, subtract, multiply, divide, negate, a mixed chain, compound assignment, a call boundary, widening, narrowing, and an excess-precision probe
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour by construction:
- No signed integer overflow. Every integer value is small and every integer result is
  far from INT_MIN and INT_MAX.
- No shift operator appears, so no shift count can be out of range.
- No division by zero, integer or floating.
- Every floating-to-integer conversion in the program has an integral part comfortably
  inside the destination's range, which is what C11 6.3.1.4p1 requires; and every
  integer-to-floating conversion is of a value exactly representable in the destination
  format, so no implementation-defined rounding decision is taken.
- No array indexing beyond bounds, no pointer arithmetic and no aliasing violation. No
  floating object is inspected byte-wise or reinterpreted through overlapping storage.
- No read of uninitialized storage: every object is initialized at its declaration and
  every volatile object has an initializer.
- No object is modified twice between sequence points.
- NOTHING DEPENDS ON UNSPECIFIED EVALUATION ORDER, and this is argued for exactly what
  the program does rather than for a stricter shape it does not have. No argument list in
  this program contains more than one volatile access: every printf argument is a plain
  local holding an already-computed result, so no call is exposed to unspecified argument
  order. The runtime variant does pair two volatile operands inside a single arithmetic
  expression -- the two operands of a binary operator, not the arguments of a call -- and
  the relative order of those two reads is indeed unspecified. The program's observable
  output cannot depend on it: the two objects are distinct, neither read modifies anything,
  no other side effect is interleaved between them, and the operator's result is the same
  whichever operand is fetched first. So both permitted orders produce the same stdout,
  which is the property the oracle needs. Pairing the operands is also what forces the
  backend to emit a genuine two-operand instruction, which is the point of the runtime
  variant.
- Hermetic, as constraint C4 requires: every input is a literal in the source. Nothing is
  opened, no socket is created, no environment variable and no program argument is read,
  and no storage is obtained from the heap.
- main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires.
- Verified empirically on this branch: the default strict warning gate
  (-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror) produces zero
  diagnostics at -O0, -O1 and -O2, and -fsanitize=undefined,address
  -fno-sanitize-recover=all runs to completion with empty stderr and exit status 0.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
FLOATING-POINT DETERMINISM rests on three deliberate choices, each verified by
measurement rather than assumed:
1. Every floating value in the program is a DYADIC RATIONAL -- an integer, or an integer
   plus a sum of negative powers of two -- so it is exactly representable in binary32 and
   binary64 alike and no rounding decision is ever taken.
2. Every printed floating value carries an explicit precision with room to spare, so no
   default precision is relied on and no digit is at the mercy of a rounding mode.
3. Excess intermediate precision cannot perturb an exact value. This matters because i686
   evaluates floating expressions in x87 extended precision (FLT_EVAL_METHOD 2) while the
   other three targets do not; the exactness of every operand and every result is what
   makes the difference unobservable.
No not-a-number, no infinity, no negative zero, no subnormal and no division by zero is
produced or assumed anywhere.

THE TWO-VARIANT RULE. Every computation is performed twice: once over constants, which
the folder evaluates at translation time, and once over volatile-qualified operands, which
must be re-read from memory at run time and so cannot be folded. Without the runtime half
the backend would never be asked to compute anything and a code-generation defect would
escape entirely; the two halves together also localise a divergence to the folder or to
the backend rather than to "one of the two".

Plain char signedness is implementation-defined and was measured as signed on x86_64 and
i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64; no plain-char value is printed. sizeof(long)
and sizeof(void *) were measured as 4 on i686 and 8 on the other three targets
(docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462); no long, size_t, ptrdiff_t, intptr_t or
pointer value is printed and no long or pointer conversion specification is used. Only
int, long long and their unsigned counterparts appear as integer destinations, each the
same width on all four targets. No address or pointer value is printed.

long double is absent entirely, its representation having been measured at 16, 12, 16 and
16 bytes across the four targets (x87 80-bit versus IEEE binary128). That type is covered
by 004_long_double_target_restricted in this area, which is the only program in the corpus
permitted to narrow a comparison on its account.

No target is dropped, no oracle is disabled and this record carries no expected-divergence
marker: a divergence here is a genuine finding. Measured on this branch with gcc 13.4.0 and the matching i686, aarch64 and riscv64 cross
drivers, executed natively and under QEMU user-mode 10.1.0: stdout is byte-identical and
the exit status is 0 in all twelve target-and-optimization-level cells.
END
